{
  "id": 242968055,
  "iid": 11677,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "Qt: Don't use winId() on a child widget (Qt Wayland issue)",
  "description": "On Qt Wayland, winId() should only be used on a top-level window:\nhttps://bugreports.qt.io/browse/QTBUG-76983\nhttps://bugreports.qt.io/browse/QTBUG-93103\nhttps://bugs.kde.org/show_bug.cgi?id=424024\nhttps://bugreports.qt.io/browse/QTBUG-75766\n    \nUsing it on the child widget and getting a native window causes the\npacket list to fail to redraw correctly when scrolling. (It does\nredraw when the window is brought to the back and then back to the front.)",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2023-08-13T10:48:06.442Z",
