        {
          "id": 1511389651,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Just spitballing, but if I understand the Wayland issue correctly it might make sense to operate on the top-level window instead, e.g.\n\n> window()->winId(); // Required for screenChanged? https://phabricator.kde.org/D20171\n> connect(window()->windowHandle(), &QWindow::screenChanged, viewport(), [=](const QScreen *) { viewport()->update(); });",
