      "parent_ids": [
        "f9f182f19edb2c0b2165afc47ca8be408d4d5bf0"
      ],
      "title": "Qt: Don't use winId() on a child widget (Qt Wayland issue)",
      "message": "Qt: Don't use winId() on a child widget (Qt Wayland issue)\n\nOn Qt Wayland, winId() should only be used on a top-level window:\nhttps://bugreports.qt.io/browse/QTBUG-76983\nhttps://bugreports.qt.io/browse/QTBUG-93103\nhttps://bugs.kde.org/show_bug.cgi?id=424024\nhttps://bugreports.qt.io/browse/QTBUG-75766\n\nUsing it on the child widget and getting a native window causes the\npacket list to fail to redraw correctly when scrolling. (It does\nredraw when the window is brought to the back and then back to the front.)\n",
      "author_name": "John Thacker",
      "author_email": "johnthacker@gmail.com",
      "authored_date": "2023-08-13T06:45:14.000-04:00",
      "committer_name": "Gerald Combs",
      "committer_email": "gerald@wireshark.org",
      "committed_date": "2023-08-15T19:23:28.000+00:00",
